From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:39:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cuda/exl3: prompt launch order, register prefetch and per-row
 rotation for GLM's routed experts (MiaAI-Lab recipe patches 0001, 0020, 0009)

Adapts Mia's (@MiaAI-Lab) prompt-window expert kernels from her GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Sparks recipe
(github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold @ 1576746, v1.5; Apache License 2.0, Copyright
2026 MiaAI-Lab) onto TensorFold's universal EXL3 routed-expert kernel, which GLM's experts use since 0.6.1. Her
patches edit GLM's dedicated kernel; here they become four launch switches of grouped_kernel, none of which changes an
output's arithmetic:

- nfirst (0001's NFIRST): grid x is the n block, so an item's n blocks run next to each other and read its member
  rows while L2 holds them ("the same kernel and arithmetic, 2.3-2.5x faster at 4,096 rows" on her kernel);
- prefetch (0001's PF): the next k step's A fragments load into registers with its trellis words (the universal
  kernel already prefetched the words), the same values into the same mma order;
- order (0020's TF_GLM_EXL3_ORDER): prompt_order_kernel lays out the grouping's (expert, 16-member tile) items with
  single-item and multi-item experts' items merged evenly (her merge arithmetic), each list in plan order; the grid
  spans only those items instead of every (expert, member tile) slot; the shared expert has no items;
- rowrot (0009's TF_GLM_EXL3_ROWROT): for a layer whose experts share one gate/up suh bit for bit (her shared_suh
  test, ported unchanged), rot_rows rotates each prompt row's input once (rot_in's arithmetic) and gate and up read the
  row (X0 = X1) instead of 2 x top_k per-pair copies.

Only GLM's call sites set them (exl3_generic.routed, which ExpertNode.compute and the attention node's local route
call), for windows of 64 rows or more (Mia's PROMPT_ROWS), from her env names: TF_GLM_EXL3_NFIRST, TF_GLM_EXL3_PF,
TF_GLM_EXL3_ORDER and TF_GLM_EXL3_ROWROT, each on by default as in her tree and =0 to turn one off. They apply to
4-bit mcg layers at GLM's tile settings (her kernel's scope); anything else, every other family and GLM's decode
windows launch as before: the off-path kernels' PTX (sm_121, -O3) is byte-identical to 0.6.5's, 79 of 79 kernels,
after name normalization. Upstream's fixes since 0.6.1 (9da0792, 682f3dc, 6245745) are untouched. The extension is
renamed tensorfold_exl3_experts_v2 (its grouped() signature changed).

Tests: tests/test_exl3_prompt_switches.py (CPU: a model of the launch covers every (expert, member tile, n block,
split, matrix) exactly once in all four orders at GLM's shapes up to 4,096 rows; a model of prompt_order_kernel gives a
permutation in plan order without the shared expert; the env and call-site plumbing; a non-GLM caller's arguments
unchanged). tests/cuda/test_exl3_prompt_switches.py (GPU: all 16 switch combinations bit-identical to the switches-off
launch at 64-2,048 rows, and the order kernel's slots equal the grouping's items).

Credit: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("GLM EXL3 prompt kernels") and the kernels' comments name MiaAI-Lab and the patches.

Co-authored-by: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (planning and execution), via Hermes

