+`rot_in_kernel`'s `ROWS`; `cuda/exl3/experts.py`: `routed(.., nfirst, prefetch, order, rowrot)`, `shared_suh`,
+`order_slots`; `families/glm5_next/cuda/exl3_generic.py`: `switches`, read from `TF_GLM_EXL3_NFIRST`, `TF_GLM_EXL3_PF`,
+`TF_GLM_EXL3_ORDER` and `TF_GLM_EXL3_ROWROT`) are adapted from MiaAI-Lab's
+[GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Spark recipe](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/tree/1576746)
+patches 0001-glm-exl3-prompt-experts (the n-first launch order and the register prefetch), 0020-glm-prompt-experts-order
+(`prompt_order_kernel`'s even merge of single-item and multi-item experts' items) and the EXL3 part of
+0009-glm-prefill-kernels (one rotated input a row for layers whose experts share one gate/up `suh`, and its
+`shared_suh` test, ported unchanged), Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 MiaAI-Lab (see
+[the license text](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)). Mia wrote them for GLM's dedicated EXL3 kernel and her prompt kernels;
+these are adaptations onto the universal kernel, not copies: an item is an (expert, 16-member tile) of the universal
+grouping, the A-fragment prefetch joins the kernel's own word prefetch, and the switches apply to 4-bit mcg layers at
+GLM's tile settings, from 64-row windows, set by GLM's call sites only. Every other launch, GLM's decode windows
+included, runs the kernels as before.
